UID:10140437-1783868400-1783879200@montclairlocal.news
SUMMARY:Opera--Rossini's Il Turco In Italia
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate 200 years of Italian opera in America — Rossini’s “Il Turco in Italia” is a madcap comedy with a touch of the surreal. A poet needs a story\, fast\, for the opera he must write\, and manipulates a colorful cast of characters to make it happen: a flirtatious heroine who has a husband\, a lover-boy\, and a visiting Turkish Bey all wrapped around her little finger (until she doesn’t). Teatro Nuovo favorites Vincent Graña and Mattia Venni return\, joined by debut artists Kresley Figueroa and Max Alexander Cook; Elisa Citterio and Derrick Goff lead the 19th-century period-instrument orchestra on violin and cembalo. \nPre-opera Serenade at 1:30pm: The Great Garcías (II): The adventure of bringing opera to the New World was bold and sometimes dangerous (think bandits in a remote Mexican mountain pass). Teatro Nuovo’s Resident Artists tell the story in music\, letters\, memoirs\, and reviews. \nPre-opera Lecture at 2:00pm: Will Crutchfield introduces “Il Turco in Italia” \nTeatro Nuovo presents Bel Canto classics and rarities with a period-instrument orchestra and a performing style the Wall Street Journal calls “transformative.” For more details\, visit TeatroNuovo.org \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
