SUMMARY:HOW WE GRIEVE Screening with Live Music & Comedy
DESCRIPTION:HOW WE GRIEVE is a new traumedy docuseries hosted by NJ-raised filmmaker siblings Meghan and Justin Ross with Austin PBS as our presenting station. On our show\, we explore all the ways people grieve in order to process our own losses and fear of our turn in the urn. Follow along on this journey as we get people to talk about the stuff no one (especially our Arab family) wants to talk about. \nJoin us on Thursday\, July 16th for a FREE public screening of our pilot episode and a sneak peek of season 1\, along with a musical performance by Brooklyn-based actor/filmmaker/singer Rozz Alizadeh Srabi and standup from Brooklyn-based comedian Ben Wasserman (featured in our pilot with his show LIVE AFTER DEATH). \nThis event is free to attend. If you’d like to help us finish season 1 for HOW WE GRIEVE’s premiere on PBS\, you can make a tax-deductible donation here. \nDoors open at 6:00pm. Event begins at 6:30pm and ends at 7:30pm. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/how-we-grieve-screening-with-live-music-comedy/
